cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-16) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: near every loop wrap of a hardware-decoded (VAAPI) video, every
    output held a frame one or more vsyncs too long (1amfwm7gq3x, PR #44).
    At the end of each pass the decoder rebuilt its surface pool while the
    render thread waited for the same VA display lock. The decode thread
    now exports each frame, the pool is built once and kept across loop
    wraps and seeks, and the render thread makes no VA call. Measured with
    8 h264 layers looping: AMD (FP530) wraps with a missed vsync 60/60 ->
    0/60; Intel N97 60/60 -> 12-25/60, one vsync each (what is left is
    GPU contention at the wrap, ticket 1amfwm7jzdq). Same pictures (CRC),
    no file descriptor or memory growth, NDI output unchanged.
  * Fixed: a hardware-decoded layer kept loaded and restarted at frame 0
    showed frame 1 (1amfwm7jme2, PR #42). A frame the decoder had not
    delivered yet was recorded as loaded; it is now asked again at the
    next vsync, without waiting.
  * Verified: 387/387 unit tests on an FP530 for this source (rc_1
    fd3e45b); rig rows on test3, the test rig's N97 node and test3 with
    NDI (cuems-RELATIONS baselines/1amfwm7gq3x). Not for show machines
    until the human test battery. Same version on every box of a cluster.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:32:13 +0100

cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-15) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: the videocomposer died when the decoding layer of a video cue
    shown on several outputs was unloaded before its shared layers, with
    software decode (ProRes, any codec VAAPI cannot decode) (1amfwm7j9r8,
    PR #39). The layer promoted to decode went on using the removed
    layer's frame memory after it was freed; it now takes that memory
    over. Hardware decode and HAP are untouched.
  * Fixed: /videocomposer/master/hue and /videocomposer/layer/<id>/hue with
    an infinite value, or one above about 8.6e9, hung the render thread for
    good: every output froze while the service stayed "active"
    (1amfwm7eyq5, PR #36). Such a value is refused with a WARNING and the
    hue is left unchanged. Text that is not a number is refused too (it
    used to count as 0, or as its leading digits).
  * A pinned refresh= never selects an interlaced mode (1amfwm7evfj, PR
    #16). refresh=30 at 1080 used to select 1080i60 without a word; it now
    takes the native progressive mode with an ERROR. An interlaced mode is
    used only when asked for with the field rate and an "i"
    (refresh=60i), or when the size has no progressive mode. The
    "refresh=... not available" WARNING lists progressive rates only.
  * Fixed: an output listed in display.conf and not connected at start
    moved, resized or blacked out the cues on the outputs that are
    (1amfwm7hrv0, PR #35). The canvas is now sized as the engine sizes
    it: every enabled section written the way cuems-generate-display-conf
    and cuems-display-setup write it counts, connected or not. A box whose
    file lists outputs it never drives gets a wider canvas (measured on an
    N97: no dropped frame, no CPU cost, at four times the width). A canvas
    the GPU cannot hold falls back to today's with an ERROR.
  * Changed: a connected monitor that display.conf does not list now stays
    dark instead of showing a copy of the canvas's top-left corner
    (1amfwm7hrv0). Exception: when no listed output is connected at all,
    the connected ones are driven as before, with an ERROR. Add an
    [output:<connector>] section to use a monitor.
  * Fixed: an output with enabled=false (or not listed) showed the Linux
    text console on boxes that have one, instead of staying dark
    (1amfwm7hrv0). It is now switched off at start.
  * The journal now says, once at start, where the engine's canvas and this
    one can still differ (grep "display.conf:"): a listed output not
    driven, a section not written in the plain form, a canvas_size line
    (still used by the engine only; ticket 1amfwm7j9xv), region lines
    without canvas_layout=custom, a connected output not listed. A file
    the generator wrote in its unknown-node fallback (every node's
    outputs, sections repeated) or one cuems-display-setup re-ran
    (duplicates kept) gets the "not written in the plain form" line at
    every start: it is true, not a fault. Boxes checked from the fleet
    records: alquiler1 (controller, node01, node02) and alquiler2
    (panera); every other box is unknown.
  * Packaging: the build fails when the binary needs an NDI library the
    package does not carry, and the bundled NDI library is shipped as the
    SDK provides it (1amfwm7j9r7, PR #38). Every package that bundled it,
    from 0.1.1-4 to 0.1.2-14, carried a stripped copy.
  * Build: no include directory outside the source tree (1amfwm7j916, PR
    #34; 1amfwm7j9r7, PR #37). The 0.1.2-14 package was compiled with a
    neighbouring libmtcmaster checkout on its include path.
  * Removed a dead class that shared its name with the display
    configuration in use (1amfwm7et2z, PR #11). No change of behaviour.
  * Verified: 373/373 unit tests on an N97 for this source (rc_1
    a1b344b), also under AddressSanitizer; rig rows per ticket on .111,
    test3 and test2 node01 (cuems-RELATIONS baselines/<ticket>). Not for
    show machines until the human test battery. Same version on every
    box of a cluster.

