cuems-videocomposer (0.1.2-14) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A video cue's first frame reaches the screen at its start (869feynrj
    4.6, PR #28). New layer command /videocomposer/layer/<id>/visible_at
    and capability token "visible_at": with 1 the layer stays hidden and
    becomes visible on the first presented frame whose content time is
    >= 0, in the same submission as that frame. Without the command
    nothing changes. Journal: "layer <id> visible at content <ms> ms" per
    reveal. Needs a cuems-engine that sends it (the release after
    0.1.0rc6-7).
  * Software-decoded layers (ProRes, any codec VAAPI cannot decode) and
    NDI:
    - Frame 0 is decoded at load, off the render thread (1amfwm7hk6j, PR
      #30). The first frame no longer holds every layer on every output
      while it decodes. Journal: "primed frame 0 of '<file>' in <ms> ms".
      Cost: about 61 ms more per load on a loader thread and one decoded
      frame kept from the load (about 8 MB at 1080p).
    - A frame uploaded from CPU memory reaches the screen in the tick it
      is chosen, once per layer (1amfwm7hg3u, PR #32). It was one refresh
      late (16.7 ms at 60 Hz), and the first draw of a layer could show
      the leftovers of another buffer. Hardware decode and HAP are
      untouched.
    - Memory leak fixed (1amfwm7hrb9, PR #31): since 0.1.2-9 every decoded
      frame leaked its compressed packet, about 8 MB/s on a 1080p30 ProRes
      layer; the videocomposer degraded after about 7 minutes.
  * Exact start for content that is not 25 fps (1amfwm7h924, PR #26). The
    engine's offset is split into whole content frames and a phase of
    less than one frame, added to the clock. A 30p cue started 0 to
    26.7 ms late depending on where the GO fell; 25p is unchanged.
  * The refresh rule in the journal (1amfwm7gq3y, PR #27). One "cadence:
    cue=<id> file=<name> <fps> fps on <hz> Hz (<connector>)" line per
    layer load: INFO when the ratio is exact; WARNING with the rate to use
    when it is not, or when a single-vsync correction comes more often
    than every 60 s (30p on 59.94 or 59.95 Hz). A pinned refresh= the sink
    cannot honour logs "refresh=... not available ... using ..." at mode
    set.
  * DRM/KMS is the default display backend (1amfwm7hjze, PR #29). DISPLAY
    and WAYLAND_DISPLAY in the environment no longer select X11 or
    Wayland: they are chosen only with --display-backend=x11|wayland. A
    backend asked for by the flag that cannot open exits with status 1
    instead of falling back; a bad value exits with status 2.
  * Test aids, off unless VIDEOCOMPOSER_CADENCE_STATS=1, never on a show:
    one "start-probe:" line per engine offset and "CpuUploadStats" every
    60 s per CPU-uploaded layer.
  * Verified: 296/296 unit tests on an FP530 and an N97 for this source
    (rc_1 78c73c9); rig rows per ticket on test3, .111 and test +
    test-node01 (cuems-RELATIONS baselines/<ticket>). Not for show
    machines until the human test battery. Same version on every box of a
    cluster.

